    "imageWidth": 2400,
    "imageHeight": 1350,
    "excerpt": "Compare rigid box construction, board specifications, opening structures and the information needed for a comparable quote.",
    "metaDescription": "Specify custom rigid boxes by product dimensions, weight, structure, board, wrap and insert. Review samples and compare like-for-like quotations.",
    "body": "*Construction descriptions are industry references as published by packaging suppliers (sources named inline); board specifications, costs and available structures must be confirmed in the quotation for the chosen product. Order terms — MOQ 200 pieces, 15–20 day production, custom sample USD 25 plus USD 20 shipping, free digital dieline previews — are ELAPACK's confirmed trade terms.*\n\n> **Quick answer:** specify a rigid box by its product dimensions, weight, opening structure, board, wrap and lining. Ask for the proposed board specification in the quote and review the assembled sample before approving production.\n\n## Key facts at a glance\n\n| Item | Figure | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Minimum order | 200 pieces | ELAPACK confirmed terms |\n| Production lead time | typically 15–20 days after sample approval and payment receipt; confirm by order | ELAPACK confirmed terms |\n| Custom sample | USD 25 plus USD 20 shipping, 3–5 days | ELAPACK confirmed terms |\n| Digital dieline preview | Free for structure approval | ELAPACK confirmed terms |\n| Board specification | Confirm material, thickness and construction for the selected design | Order quotation and approved sample |\n| Cost comparison | Compare the same dimensions, quantity, structure and finishes | Like-for-like quotations |\n\n## How buyers name rigid boxes\n\nA rigid-box enquiry should name the proposed construction, opening style and product dimensions. A search term such as “rigid mailer” does not establish its material or shipping suitability. The cross-section is an illustrative wrapped-board construction; confirm the actual build on the quotation and sample. Compare decoration separately in the [surface finishes guide](https://elapack.com/news/surface-finishes-compared-guide/).\n\n**Rigid boxes are ordered by construction, not by occasion — name the build in the enquiry, not the gift.**\n\n## The three-layer build\n\nFor a wrapped-board construction, identify the structural core, external wrap and any internal lining. [Zenpack’s guide](https://www.zenpack.us/blog/custom-rigid-box-packaging/) describes a greyboard core and wrap paper; this is a supplier construction example, not proof that every rigid box has identical layers or recycled content. Confirm material identification, thickness, wrap, lining and the assembled design for your product.\n\n**Choose the board with the structure and product; confirm the specification before artwork approval.**\n\n## Structure shortlist and product examples\n\nA shortlist can include a [magnetic flip-top](https://elapack.com/products/magnetic-closure-gift-box/), a [ribbon-tie box](https://elapack.com/products/luxury-gift-box-ribbon/) or a lid-and-base structure. Magnetic closure is a closure choice within a box construction, rather than a material category. Confirm availability, assembly and fit for the selected design.\n\n## Rigid mailers\n\nA presentation box is not automatically suitable as a shipping outer. Assess the loaded product, insert, closure, outer carton and intended parcel route together. Agree on sample transport checks and acceptance criteria before approving bulk production. The [packaging inserts guide](https://elapack.com/news/packaging-inserts-guide/) covers product restraint.\n\n**Approve the complete shipping pack against the intended route before relying on its protective performance.**\n\n## Wrap, lining and what drives cost\n\nThree cost levers sit above the board: the wrap (art paper, specialty paper, textile), the finish set on it (lamination, foil, emboss — compared in the finishes guide), and the lining. Ask for comparable quotations with the same board, wrap, finish, insert and quantity. For assembly, agree on the dimensions, closure fit and inspection records required for your order. Structures and stock formats across the range sit on the [boxes collection](https://elapack.com/products/?category=Boxes) and the [custom gift boxes](https://elapack.com/custom-gift-boxes/) page.\n\n## What to put in your enquiry\n\nA rigid enquiry a factory can quote first time carries: the proposed structure or a drawing; the greyboard grade — or the product and weight and let the factory propose; wrap and finish choices; internal layout, cross-referenced to the insert specification; quantity against the 200-piece minimum; vector artwork; and the sample route. A digital dieline preview is provided free for approval against confirmed product dimensions, covered in the [die cutting and dielines guide](https://elapack.com/news/die-cutting-and-dielines-guide/).\n\n## The bottom line\n\nPick the grade for the weight, the structure for the opening, and let wrap and finish carry the brand. [Contact ELAPACK](https://elapack.com/contact/) with the product, structure and quantity, and the quotation will state board grade, wrap, tooling and terms that apply."
