    "metaDescription": "Compare paperboard, corrugated, foam, moulded-pulp and thermoformed insert proposals. Confirm material, cavity design, loaded fit and sample scope.",
    "body": "*Material classifications and trade-offs are industry references as published by packaging suppliers (sources named inline); the material families below are design candidates, not verified ELAPACK product lines or savings claims. Confirm the selected material, construction and price for your order. Order terms — MOQ 200 pieces, 15–20 day production — are ELAPACK's confirmed trade terms.*\n\n> **Quick answer:** compare insert designs against product dimensions, weight, fragility and removal. Ask suppliers to specify the material and cavity construction, quote comparable alternatives and provide a loaded sample. Space, cost and protection depend on the complete design; no fixed saving applies across orders.\n\n## Key facts at a glance\n\n| Item | Figure | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Minimum order | 200 pieces | ELAPACK confirmed terms |\n| Production lead time | typically 15–20 days after sample approval and payment receipt; confirm by order | ELAPACK confirmed terms |\n| Material and construction | Confirm the proposed material, grade and cavity design | Order quotation and sample |\n| Space and cost | Compare complete designs with the same product and requirements | Dimensions and like-for-like quotations |\n\n## Fitments and insert cards: one enquiry, two line items\n\nSeparate structural fitments that support the product from printed cards that carry care information or messages. Both may share the box interior, but they need not use the same drawing or be ordered together. Coordinate the actual dimensions and placement. The outer construction is covered in the [rigid-box guide](https://elapack.com/news/custom-rigid-boxes-guide/).\n\n**Coordinate the fitment, any card and the usable box interior; record separate component references where needed.**\n\n## The material systems side by side\n\n[Wynalda’s insert guide](https://www.wynalda.com/2026/02/17/custom-packaging-inserts-types-and-examples/) describes paperboard, corrugated, moulded-pulp, thermoformed and foam examples. [Custom Box Makers](https://www.customboxmakers.com/custom-box-inserts/) also lists paperboard, corrugated, EVA and PU foam among its options. These are supplier-published examples, not an exhaustive standard or ELAPACK production list. Confirm the actual material, grade and construction proposed for your order.\n\n| Candidate system | Construction to identify | Sample or quote question |\n|---|---|---|\n| Paperboard | Die-cut sheet, folds and supports | How does the loaded design retain and release the product? |\n| Corrugated | Flute, board construction and supports | What board and cavity design is proposed? |\n| Foam | Polymer, grade, density and cut geometry | What contact and movement checks apply? |\n| Layered board | Layers, bonding and cavity | What dimensions and assembly are proposed? |\n| Moulded pulp | Fibre formulation and formed geometry | What tooling, sample scope and quantity apply? |\n| Thermoformed | Polymer, sheet gauge and formed geometry | What contact, removal and appearance checks apply? |\n\n*These are design options to discuss with the supplier, not a confirmed ELAPACK production-range statement. Compare the proposed specification and sample.*\n\n**Shortlist by the product and packing requirements, then review the proposed sample.**\n\n## The rule that decides: weight, fragility, lift\n\nChoose an insert using product dimensions, weight, fragility, surface sensitivity and how the item is removed. Material names alone do not establish load capacity, cost or transit protection. Compare proposed designs using the same product and review a loaded sample through the [sample process](https://elapack.com/news/custom-packaging-samples-guide/). A pillow for a watch, platform for lashes or layered-board cavity are possible design briefs, not verified specifications of the linked catalogue products. Confirm the actual insert separately for a [watch box](https://elapack.com/products/custom-watch-boxes/), [eyelash box](https://elapack.com/products/custom-eyelash-packaging-boxes/) or [magnetic box](https://elapack.com/products/magnetic-closure-gift-box/). The [custom watch boxes guide](https://elapack.com/news/custom-watch-boxes-guide/) covers structures and personalisation in detail.\n\n**Review dimensions, weight, surface sensitivity, movement and removal together on the loaded sample.**\n\n## Insert cards: the quiet second intent\n\n\"Packaging insert cards\" names its own line item: care cards, warranty cards, gift messages. They are specified like any printed component — board weight, size against the fitment's slot, artwork, Pantones — and they fail in one predictable way: ordered at a size that does not slot into the final fitment. Specify the card with the fitment, not after it. For colour approvals across card and fitment, record each component's reference, viewing conditions and approved sample as described in the [colour review guide](https://elapack.com/news/packaging-colour-tolerance-explained/).\n\n## Worked examples in the range\n\nThe [candle boxes guide](https://elapack.com/news/custom-candle-boxes-guide/) covers vessel fit and insert questions. Related multi-component presentations sit in the [sets collection](https://elapack.com/products/?category=Sets%20%26%20Complete%20Packaging); the [tissue guide](https://elapack.com/news/custom-tissue-paper-guide/) covers the separate wrapping component. Confirm availability and fit for the selected project.\n\n## What to put in your enquiry\n\nAn insert enquiry a factory can quote first time carries: the product's dimensions and weight; fragility notes (glass, plating, scratch-sensitive faces); the box it goes into; the lift requirement — how the piece is removed and by whom; the material system or a request for proposals across two; card slot requirements if insert cards ride along; and quantity against the 200-piece minimum. Sculpted foam cavities are cut to the confirmed product drawing, so product drawings come before insert quotations.\n\n## The bottom line\n\nCompare the proposed paper, foam or layered-board construction on the same product and requirements, and specify any card with the cavity. [Contact ELAPACK](https://elapack.com/contact/) with the product drawing, weight and box format, and the quotation will state the insert system, cavity layout and terms that apply."
